   170	## 3. Graph-deployment verification (plan 0.3)
   171	"Zero graph breaks" is not accepted as evidence of full capture. For C1, C3,
   172	H (Inductor cudagraph trees) and B, E, G (manual graphs), record per pass,
   173	from the node-level nsys export of session 2 (`cuda_api_trace` +
   174	`cuda_gpu_trace`, capture window = the 5a latency block):
   175	`cudaGraphLaunch` calls/pass, `cudaLaunchKernel`-family calls/pass outside
   176	graph replay (eager launches), memcpy/memset API calls/pass, distinct kernel
   177	names inside vs outside replay; plus, for the Inductor arms, the
   178	`torch._inductor` cudagraph counters (`cudagraph_skips` and reasons,
   179	`TORCH_LOGS=cudagraphs`) and the cudagraph-trees recorded-graph count.
   180	Launch counts include runtime AND driver entry points (`cudaLaunchKernel`,
   181	`cudaLaunchKernelExC`, `cuLaunchKernel`, `cuLaunchKernelEx`; `cudaGraphLaunch`
   182	/ `cuGraphLaunch`). This nsys version's GPU trace carries no graph-id column
   183	even under `--cuda-graph-trace=node`, so GPU events are attributed by
   184	CorrId correlation: a kernel whose CorrId belongs to a graph-launch API call
   185	is captured; to a kernel-launch call, eager; neither → UNRESOLVED (counted,
   186	never assumed captured). API calls are windowed by the CPU-side NVTX pass
   187	range, kernels by the GPU-projected range. Fourfold classification per pass: (i) captured
   188	model computation (kernels inside replay); (ii) uncaptured model computation;
   189	(iii) external input staging (cudagraph-trees copies of non-static inputs
   190	into the static pool — `_foreach_copy_`/copy kernels/`cudaMemcpyAsync`);
   191	(iv) other uncaptured copies/memsets. Also reported: recorded-graph count
   192	(Inductor counters), graphs visited per pass, replay launches per pass, and
   193	compile/recording counter stability across settle → validation → timing.
   194	An arm is **fully graphed** only with positive replay evidence (≥1 graph
   195	launch in EVERY captured pass) AND zero uncaptured model kernels AND zero
   196	unresolved kernels in every pass (medians hide a defective minority); the
   197	captured pass count must equal the requested 50. Multiple graphs per pass
   198	are legitimate; staging (`_foreach_copy_`/multi_tensor_apply, direct-copy
   199	kernels, memcpy) is timed overhead but not uncaptured model work; bare
   200	elementwise kernels are model work.
   201	Arms verified: C1, C3, H (Inductor) and B, E, G (manual), from their
   202	session-2 traces at both operating points. No expectation is registered.
   203	
   204	## 4. Boundary-cost microbenchmark (plan 0.4; design registered, owner reviews)
   205	`fullmodel/boundary_bench.py`: chains of N **dependent** kernels, N ∈ {10,
   206	100, 1000, 2000}: (trivial) one Triton program loads ONE int32 element, adds
   207	1, stores it back to the same buffer — kernel k+1 depends on kernel k, and
   208	the final counter must equal the total launch count (exact-integer
   209	dependency proof); (elem37) an in-place value-preserving fp16 elementwise op
   210	on a 37 MB tensor, N ∈ {10, 100}; (gemm) alternating dependent GEMMs
   211	660×384×1536 / 660×1536×384 fp16 into preallocated ping-pong outputs with
   212	1/√K-scaled weights (bounded values), N ∈ {10, 100}. Modes: stream launches;
   213	one CUDA graph of the chain (replayed); programmatic dependent launch for the
   214	trivial chain (Triton 3.4 `launch_pdl=True`; `gdc_wait()` before the
   215	dependent load, `gdc_launch_dependents()` after the store; the PTX is checked
   216	for `griddepcontrol`), on a stream and inside a graph; real-kernel PDL is
   217	UNSUPPORTED through cuBLAS/ATen launches and recorded as such. Note: the
   218	triton 3.4.0 wheel's `language/extra/cuda/gdc.py` carries the pre-3.4
   219	`_builder=` signature and fails to compile under the 3.4 code generator
   220	(`_semantic=`); the bench therefore defines the same two one-line PTX
   221	intrinsics with the 3.4 signature (identical asm strings) — recorded here
   222	so the deviation from the library call is explicit. The elem37 chain's
   223	working set (37 MB) fits the RTX 5090's 96 MiB L2, so that chain measures
   224	the L2-resident rate, which is reported as the plan-1.4 L2 bandwidth input. Timing:
   225	unprofiled device time via CUDA events around the chain, median of 20
   226	repeats with min/max → `T(N)` per (chain, mode), plus least-squares slope
   227	and intercept over N. **`T(N)/N` and the slope are effective per-node service
   228	times INCLUDING kernel execution — not boundary costs.** A separate
   229	node-level trace of the same script yields, per chain segment (NVTX), the
   230	median kernel duration and the median serial inter-kernel gap; for non-PDL
   231	modes the serial gap is the boundary estimate; for PDL modes kernels overlap
   232	and no subtraction is attempted (pure boundary `UNRESOLVED`); the traced
   233	run's perturbation vs the unprofiled `T(N)` is reported. Prior calibration
   234	points to compare against: Hazy (H100 ≈ 2.1 µs stream, ≈ 1.3 µs graph);
   235	NVIDIA's CUDA 12.6 figure ≈ 0.55 µs/node is empty-kernel graph device
   236	service time (RTX 3060), not CPU launch cost. **Until measured, no
   237	per-boundary number is used anywhere**, and the ledger's X10 must not count
   238	kernel execution as removable boundary overhead. Trace-derived gaps are
   239	accepted only for segments whose qualification case exists in the traced
   240	run's own JSON with a passed dependency proof and PTX verdict and whose
   241	NVTX segment holds exactly N × 20 kernels (a missing qualification file
   242	yields no calibration value at all); the perturbation runs (plan 1.6) are
   243	accepted only when all three runs are VALID, validation PASS, one block
   244	holding exactly 50 recorded passes, manifest-bound with the same recorded
   245	effective variant, and (compiled arms) affirmatively recording-stable —
   246	otherwise EVERY derived ratio and the caveat are cleared to UNRESOLVED. Any
   247	unavailable mode is recorded `UNTESTED(reason)`.
   248	
   249	## 5. Session structure, protocol, budget
   250	- **Protocol 5a**, reused from `arms/common.py::timed_run` (per-iteration
   251	  synchronize latency block of 50 passes inside the cudaProfilerApi range;
   252	  one free-running block of 50 passes outside it), **five repeats per
   253	  process**; per-process statistic = min-of-medians and median spread; per
   254	  (arm × chunk) headline = **median over 3 fresh-process restarts of the
   255	  per-process min-of-medians**, every per-iteration list preserved
   256	  (an explicit extension of `sm120` README deviation 5; spread = max − min of
   257	  the repeat medians; within-process and between-process variation are both
   258	  preserved). **Plan 1.2 matched comparisons** use `fullmodel/matched_run.py`:
   259	  two arms built, settled and validated in ONE fresh process, then their 5a
   260	  blocks ALTERNATE (a, b, a, b, …, five each) so every block pair is matched
   261	  in time and clocks; repeated in three fresh processes. Registered pairs at
   262	  352800: (C1, C3) the graph-break tax; (C1, C1D) the DC-filter repair
   263	  alone; (C3, H) the pad-and-batch delta; (C1, C1A) once, to record the
   264	  expected compile failure. The matrix restarts are additionally round-major
   265	  (r1 of every arm, then r2, then r3). Clocks logged in the background at
   266	  1 Hz with timestamp and GPU UUID (`nvidia-smi --query-gpu=timestamp,uuid,
   267	  clocks.sm,clocks.mem,power.draw,temperature.gpu,utilization.gpu -l 1`) for
   268	  the whole session; timed blocks carry wall timestamps.
   269	  **Matched-pair acceptance:** both builds OK, both graph gates PASS, no
   270	  capped settle, a JOINT settle of the actual alternation (counters stable
   271	  across two full alternation rounds), both validations PASS after the joint
   272	  settle, counters stable across every block, and — joined at collection —
   273	  SDR PASS for both arms' cells at that operating point; otherwise the pair
   274	  is ineligible with reasons.
   275	  **Compile/recording stability:** a compiled run is eligible only if, across
   276	  settle → validation → timing → SDR, there are no new graph breaks or
   277	  unimplemented ops, the unique-graph count is unchanged, and every Inductor
   278	  cudagraph counter (recordings, skips, non-static-input recordings) is
   279	  unchanged; all snapshots are preserved in the run JSON.
   280	  **Provenance gate:** every process verifies the msst clone (HEAD = pin,
   281	  clean), the checkpoint sha256, the registered config path and the
   282	  explicit `use_amp` before building; the session preflight writes ONE
   283	  immutable `session_manifest.json` (repo commit + clean tree, sha256 of
   284	  this registration, of every measuring file, the clip manifest, pins,
   285	  environment) that every run and every reference is bound to; a mismatch
   286	  refuses the run.
   287	  **Headline rule:** a cell publishes a headline only if restarts r1, r2 AND
   288	  r3 all exist and are eligible (EXACTLY the 5×50 protocol, validation PASS,
   289	  recording state stable, manifest-bound, not a planted/traced/attribution
   290	  run), share ONE session manifest and ONE effective variant (capture scope
   291	  / adapter / compile mode / stream count), and the cell's SDR qualification
   292	  — taken only from the r1 record, same manifest and variant — is PASS; a
   293	  failed required restart is never replaced by a later tag. A matched pair
   294	  publishes a pair headline only if m1, m2 AND m3 are pair-eligible (5×50,
   295	  three matched restarts) under one manifest with one variant pair and both
   296	  arms' cells hold that SDR qualification; the matched runner re-checks each
   297	  arm's recording state after the joint settle and after validation.
   298	  **Recording observer:** compiled runs snapshot the cudagraph-trees
   299	  manager identity, the identity set of its recorded graph nodes (roots and
   300	  descendants) and its function-id set together with the dynamo/inductor
   301	  counters at every phase boundary; stability means every one of these is
   302	  unchanged (sets compared, never counts); a missing observer leaves
   303	  stability UNRESOLVED and the run ineligible.
   304	  **Independent qualification:** every publisher (driver, matched runner,
   305	  collector, completeness audit) re-derives eligibility from the record
   306	  itself through one versioned validator (`fullmodel/qualify.py`); stored
   307	  eligibility flags are never trusted, and a record whose stored flag
   308	  contradicts the validator — in either direction — is ineligible. The
   309	  validator checks payloads, not labels: both registered validation seeds
   310	  with finite per-pass differences under the arm's registered tier
   311	  tolerances, the SDR gate recomputed from exactly eight distinct finite
   312	  clip rows against the registered threshold, recording stability
   313	  recomputed from the stored phase snapshots (and, for matched pairs, from
   314	  every phase transition: joint settle, validation, every block), the
   315	  zero-break gate's counter for C3/H. Every published statistic (block
   316	  medians, min-of-medians, restart spread, throughput, matched deltas) is
   317	  recomputed from the recorded samples, which must be finite and positive;
   318	  a stored summary that differs from its samples disqualifies the record.
   319	  Each run persists the sha256 of every reference artifact its lineage
   320	  check saw; the three restarts of a cell must have been validated against
   321	  the same hashed validation references (r1 alone additionally checks the
   322	  eager-A clip outputs). The completeness audit re-derives every cell and
   323	  pair from the run records through the same validator (never from the
   324	  collector's summary), re-hashes every reference sidecar, and requires the
   325	  clock log to span every timing block.
   326	  **Runtime pins and manifest scope:** every process checks torch ==
   327	  2.8.0+cu128 and triton == 3.4.0 before building; the manifest binds the
   328	  complete measuring set (fullmodel/**, arms/*, scripts/*, configs/*,
   329	  frontend.py, frontend_rms_fused.py, setup.sh, this registration, the
   330	  runtime identity) and is compared field by field on every load; every
   331	  reference artifact (validation outputs, eager-A clip outputs) carries its
   332	  own lineage sidecar (manifest id + sha256) checked before use.
   333	- **Unprofiled timing is the primary result.** Session-2 traces are for
   334	  mechanism; profiled and unprofiled numbers never share a ratio. Profiling
   335	  perturbation (plan 1.6): A, C3, G at 4410 and 352800, wall unprofiled vs
   336	  `--cuda-graph-trace=graph` vs `=node`; >5 % inflation → every mechanism
   337	  number from that trace carries the factor as a caveat.
   338	- **Session 1 (≤ 3 h, RunPod secure-cloud RTX 5090, pod name
   339	  `melband_profiling`, image `runpod/pytorch:1.1.0-rc.154-cu1281-torch280-ubuntu2204`
   340	  = the pinned torch 2.8.0+cu128 / triton 3.4.0 matrix):** in this order —
   341	  setup (idempotent `setup.sh` + clip pack + nsys check); eager-A references
   342	  at both operating points; the two planted-fault checks; C3 operator
   343	  qualification per frame count; the matched pairs (§5, plan 1.2); the arm
   344	  matrix at 352800 and 4410 (three round-major restarts, SDR gate in r1 at
