   412	  graph verification requires an affirmative node-level export record and
   413	  exactly the registered 50 passes (any other expected count is an
   414	  unregistered shakedown; a missing record is UNRESOLVED); for the eager
   415	  and multi-stream arms (A, D, F) the expected qualified verdict is
   416	  NO_REPLAY_EVIDENCE; timing views count kernels only (memcpy/memset rows
   417	  are reported separately as memops); the recording observer assigns
   418	  lifetime-safe identities through a weak registry (address-based
   419	  identities leave stability UNRESOLVED);
   420	  boundary microbench (§4) plus its node-level trace and traced-vs-unprofiled
   421	  perturbation; per-kernel ideal costs (plan 1.4) computed only from the
   422	  compiled variant(s) whose ORDERED per-pass Triton sequence is reproduced
   423	  by a UNIQUE decomposition into compiled-graph call sequences (graphs may
   424	  repeat; graphs are interchangeable only when their complete pricing
   425	  semantics agree — kernel body hashes, access sites, iteration literals,
   426	  argument shapes/strides/types and every extern/fallback call in order; graphs without Triton kernels are invisible to the
   427	  decomposition and are stated as such; SDPA call count reconciled exactly,
   428	  GEMM events ≥ extern calls, captured pass count = 50; zero or several
   429	  decompositions → UNRESOLVED, expected for graph-broken arms such as C1/C2
   430	  whose per-graph kernel numbering makes names non-unique). Inductor GEMM
   431	  template kernels (`triton_tem_*`, max-autotune) are counted in the GEMM
   432	  class and are not priced by the byte model. Registered deviations from a literal
   433	  per-kernel FLOPs/bytes table: cuBLAS kernel names carry no shapes, so GEMM
   434	  ideals are computed per extern call site from the wrapper and compared at
   435	  class level; SDPA ideals are class-level (12 calls/pass at the model
   436	  shapes); Inductor fused pointwise/reduction kernels are priced by bytes
   437	  only (bandwidth bound, zero FLOPs) with per-call L2 residency tests. Byte
   438	  model for a fused kernel call: per pointer argument, element size from the
   439	  kernel's own ABI signature (`triton_meta`), traffic = min(distinct
   440	  elements of the argument's strided footprint, load/store sites × the
   441	  call's iteration space) × element size, reads and writes charged
   442	  separately, where the iteration space is the product of the call's
   443	  positional integer literals bound one-to-one to the kernel's numeric
   444	  parameters (any other call form is UNRESOLVED); the L2 residency test
   445	  uses the union of the distinct base allocations the call touches, each at
   446	  its full allocated size (an over-estimate: a call passes the test only
   447	  when its whole working set provably fits — allocation size is the address
   448	  extent from the base allocation's own shape, stride and dtype, unknown →
   449	  no L2 ideal); every measured value comes from exactly 50 non-empty
   450	  validated per-pass windows (the aggregate kernel summary is reconciled
   451	  against them by name set, count and duration, differences reported), and
   452	  an arm whose windows are not the registered 50 passes publishes no rows;
   453	  boundary calibration accepts a segment only when its case carries a passed
   454	  dependency-proof counter (trivial chains) and, for PDL modes, the PTX
   455	  qualification — labels alone never qualify; source-map coverage credits
   456	  only exact, unambiguous kernel names with resolved fused ops; graph-input dtypes from the wrapper's benchmark section;
   457	  fallback-op outputs from their `assert_size_stride`. This over-counts
   458	  slice reads, so a row whose HBM-model ideal exceeds its measured time is
   459	  flagged `bound_not_tight` and its recoverable share under the HBM model is
   460	  0 (never negative, never inflated); eager ATen fallbacks, cuFFT and copy
   461	  kernels without wrapper shapes stay UNRESOLVED. A kernel → fused-op source
   462	  map with its coverage share accompanies the table; exports; evidence
   463	  extraction. Session 2 runs under the
   464	  same deadline/reserve/terminal-record rules as session 1 (qualification
   465	  and microbenchmarks included).
   466	  **Plan 1.7 dependency model (registered):** the exports carry no event or
   467	  graph edges, so the critical-path view is the OBSERVED-ORDER longest chain
   468	  of pairwise non-overlapping kernels (edge a→b iff a ended before b
   469	  started); it is an upper bound on the true dependency path, satisfies
